00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:23.500
Now, speaking of background groundwater concentrations, here's something I wish someone had told

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:29.420
me early in my career. You arrive at a former industrial site in southern Ontario for the first

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:37.140
post spring thoughts sampling round. MW4 shows benzene at 18 micrograms per liter while the same

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:44.280
well read 4 micrograms per liter in January yet no new release is suspected. The difference is

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:50.200
almost entirely driven by water table fluctuation and temperature driven biodegradation rates rather

00:03:50.200 --> 00:04:01.020
than plume migration. Under OREG 153-04 and CCME Tier 1, background wells must be sampled at the

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:07.320
same frequency and analytical suite as compliance wells. Failure to capture this seasonal envelope

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:20.020
often leads to unnecessary delineation or incorrect statistical trend analysis. Experience

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:25.560
are attributing concentration shifts to site sources. The most common mistake is treating a

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:31.660
single low flow event as representative without checking whether the well screen intersects the

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:38.360
seasonal high water table. The fix is to schedule at least one additional event during the opposite

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:45.580
hydrologic extreme before finalizing the conceptual site model. If you're working on active Ontario

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:52.480
and BC sites, review the current CCME soil vapor draft for any proposed changes to attenuation

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:58.740
factors. Update internal holding time trackers to align with upcoming federal carbon pricing

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:06.020
benchmark revisions effective 1st July. Monitor Canada Gazette Part 1 for any CEPA 2024

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:12.840
amendment notices published in the next 10 days. Brief project managers on the absence of new

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:19.080
enforcement actions so that existing compliance schedules remain the priority. Mark your calendar

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:25.660
for 22nd June when the CCME soil vapor guideline comment period closes at the federal level.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:33.540
Note 30th June as the BC CSR schedule 2 annual compliance reporting deadline for sites with

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:39.740
active certificates of compliance. The federal output based pricing system benchmark adjustment

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:45.180
takes effect on 1st July in all provinces without equivalent provincial systems.

